WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.474
Kubernetes deployment scripts often run in
CI/CD systems.

2
00:00:03.554 --> 00:00:06.826
That means runner permissions, branch
filters, protected tags,

3
00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:10.534
environment gates, approval workflows, and
secret scoping all matter.

4
00:00:10.614 --> 00:00:14.778
A runner that can deploy to production
should be treated as a sensitive operational

5
00:00:14.858 --> 00:00:15.393
identity.

6
00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:18.566
The pipeline should make it clear which
branches, tags, jobs,

7
00:00:18.646 --> 00:00:21.442
and approvals can trigger changes in each
environment.

8
00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:24.853
Logs should support review without
exposing sensitive material.

9
00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:27.371
Useful deployment logs show which identity
ran,

10
00:00:27.451 --> 00:00:31.496
which cluster and namespace were targeted,
which version or image was deployed,

11
00:00:31.576 --> 00:00:34.015
what action occurred, and whether it
succeeded.

12
00:00:34.095 --> 00:00:38.318
Logs should avoid tokens, kubeconfig
contents, Secrets, sensitive manifest data,

13
00:00:38.398 --> 00:00:39.707
and excessive raw output.

14
00:00:39.787 --> 00:00:42.225
Operators need enough context to
troubleshoot,

15
00:00:42.305 --> 00:00:45.101
but not a second copy of sensitive
deployment material.

16
00:00:45.181 --> 00:00:48.988
Monitoring should detect failed
deployments, repeated rollout failures,

17
00:00:49.068 --> 00:00:51.745
unexpected namespace changes, unusual
identities,

18
00:00:51.825 --> 00:00:53.668
drift from approved configuration,

19
00:00:53.748 --> 00:00:56.901
and deployment activity outside expected
windows or sources.

20
00:00:56.981 --> 00:01:00.728
These signals help teams catch both
reliability issues and control drift.

21
00:01:00.808 --> 00:01:04.972
A deployment script should produce status
that monitoring and operations can use,

22
00:01:05.052 --> 00:01:07.907
not only console text that disappears
after the job ends.

23
00:01:07.987 --> 00:01:11.199
Periodic review should cover scripts,
RBAC, service accounts,

24
00:01:11.279 --> 00:01:14.194
kubeconfig storage, CI/CD variables,
deployment gates,

25
00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:17.664
image promotion rules, logging behavior,
and rollback readiness.

26
00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:21.254
Incidents and failed rollouts should feed
back into better controls.

27
00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:24.129
Secure deployment scripting is not a
one-time project;

28
00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:28.432
it is an operational practice that
improves as teams learn where their automation is

29
00:01:28.512 --> 00:01:29.940
fragile or overprivileged.
